  "term": "social deprivation",
  "definition": "Social deprivation is a lack of access to a society’s resources because of poverty, discrimination, or other disadvantage. It is often described using demographic indicators such as poverty, low education, single-parent households, rented or overcrowded housing, lack of a car, and unemployment among adults under 65.",
